contentText:
Stray Kids are speechless. The members of the K-pop supergroup reacted on Sunday night (Aug. 16) to the news that their latest release, THIS & THAT is officially their ninth Billboard chart-topper .

&#8220;Hello all, we are Stray Kids!,&#8221; the eight-member group said in unison in an Instagram Story captioned, &#8220;9th consecutive Billboard 200 #1 album &#8216;THIS & THAT&#8217; &#8230; Thank you STAY, from the bottom of our hearts.&#8221;

&#8220;Today we are excited to share the most exciting news ever,&#8221; added member Bang Chan. &#8220;Our most recent album, THIS & THAT , has reached No. 1 on the Billboard 200 for the ninth consecutive time! Unbelievable!&#8221;

Singer Felix added, &#8220;We are deeply grateful for all of your support. Thank you so much STAY. Without you, we wouldn&#8217;t have been able to achieve this incredible milestone. So we&#8217;d like to cherish this moment together with you and with everyone, everywhere all around the world.&#8221;

After a message in Korean, Seungmin concluded by saying, &#8220;Thank you for enjoying all our different sides, from this to that. We hope you look forward to spending the rest of the year with us as well.&#8221;

