The group did have plenty to celebrate, as their ninth No. 1 album topped the chart dated Aug. 22, earning 369,000 equivalent album units in the U.S. in the week ending Aug. 13, according to Luminate, which marked the crew&#8217;s biggest week by units to date. Of that number, traditional album sales comprised 357,000, marking the act&#8217;s best sales week ever.

The eight-track THIS & THAT ’s album sales were helped by its availability across 17 CD and vinyl variants, all of which contain collectibles including photocards, posters and stickers, as well as eight digital download variants.

All nine of the group’s&nbsp; Billboard 200 &nbsp;chart entries have debuted at No. 1, starting with&nbsp; ODDINARY &nbsp;in 2022. Then, in 2024,&nbsp; HOP &nbsp;also debuted at the top, making Stray Kids the first act to debut its first six entries at No. 1. With their 9th entry, Stray Kids extend their record for the most No. 1s among groups this century (since 2000), as well as tying the Rolling Stones for the second-most No. 1s on the Billboard 200 among groups; The Beatles lead all acts with 19 No. 1s. They also have set a record for the most No. 1 albums by a K-pop group of all time.

The Stray Kids&#8217; 2026 RUN IT world tour is slated to touch down at Tokyo&#8217;s National Stadium on Aug. 29 before the crew heads down to South America in September for shows in Colombia, Brazil and Argentina, as well as two nights (Sept. 25-26) at Estadio GNP Seguros in Mexico City.
